 "poem": "Though, in a little walk by river,\nThe lovers' love was sharpest to behold;\nBut 'twere not their rosy lips they ever\nMay show the morning's fullst of emotion.\nYet some immortal hero ever\nAnd their martyr's prayer could quiet our\nLong-trodden thoughts - ere the lyre began her\nDebut, and the world sang England's renown;\nAnd henceforth, heal'd from all our grief,\nSoon more than he may seem, as our\nPoor piteous souls, shall hear again indeed\nThy immortal lines his tender power",
